[31.001, "o", "e"]
[31.022, "o", "."]
[31.042, "o", "\r\n"]
[34.57, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u25cf drain_node\u001b[0m\u001b[2m({\"node\": \"k8s-w1\", \"reason\": \"ReadonlyFilesystem: EXT4-fs (vda1) remounted read-only; suspected disk fault, pending hardware check\"})\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[34.693, "o", "    \u001b[2m\u2514\u001b[0m \u001b[32mdone\u001b[0m  kubectl cordon k8s-w1 && kubectl annotate node k8s-w1 slurm-k8s-lab/triage-reason=\"triage: ReadonlyFilesystem: EXT4-fs (vda1) remounted read-only; suspected disk fault, pending hardware check\"\r\n"]
[34.693, "o", "    \u001b[2m\u2514\u001b[0m cordoned: nothing new is scheduled; running pods stay until drained\r\n"]
[39.575, "o", "\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  k8s-w1 is now cordoned (`done: true`). The tool ran:\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  \r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  ```\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  kubectl cordon k8s-w1 && kubectl annotate node k8s-w1 slurm-k8s-lab/triage-reason=\"triage:\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  ReadonlyFilesystem: EXT4-fs (vda1) remounted read-only; suspected disk fault, pending hardware check\"\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  ```\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  \r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  No new pods will be scheduled there. The 11 pods already on the node are still running on the read-only\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  disk until you evict them. The reason annotation should also make it clear why the node is out, so it's\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  less likely to be uncordoned by mistake like it was at 21:49.\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  \r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  **What's left for you:**\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  1. **Check that CoreDNS can move before you evict.** Both replicas are on k8s-w1, so make sure other nodes\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  have room for them. Then run:\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "     ```\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "     kubectl drain k8s-w1 --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data --timeout=5m\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "     ```\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "     If a PodDisruptionBudget blocks the drain, it needs capacity elsewhere or an agreed disruption. Don't\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  delete pods to get past it.\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  2. **Check the disk before any reboot:**\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "     ```\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "     ssh k8s-w1 \"dmesg -T | grep -iE 'I/O error|remount|EXT4-fs error'\"\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "     ```\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "     Also check the SMART data. If the disk is failing, open a hardware ticket. Only fsck and reboot if it\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  isn't.\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  3. **slurm-c1** still needs its hardware ticket for the missing GPU (3 of 4 registered). It's already\r\n"]
[39.576, "o", "  drained, so nothing needs to be done in the scheduler.\r\n"]
[40.191, "o", "\r\n"]
[40.192, "o", "\u001b[2m   Slinky (Slurm on Kubernetes) reacts to the cordon on its own:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[40.192, "o", "\u001b[32m$\u001b[0m "]
[40.192, "o", "k"]
